     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":3,\"rationale\":\"Blocking browserStore:credentialAccess, printServer:lateralMovement and backupHost:lateralMovement makes the target unreachable, and no 2-step block works. (1) Blocking browserStore cuts off dbLogin, vpnSession and appServer, because each needs browserStore. Without dbLogin, domainAdmin (an AND step) fails, and so dbReplica fails. (2) Blocking printServer cuts off hypervisor (an AND step that needs printServer). With appServer, domainAdmin and hypervisor gone, codeRepo has no live parent. (3) Blocking backupHost cuts off serviceAccount and secretsManager (both AND steps that need backupHost), so vaultRead fails. With printServer and backupHost blocked, shareMount has no live parent. All four parents of crownData are then dead. Why 2 is not enough: shareMount is reachable through printServer, which tokenCache feeds from the vpnGateway foothold, and through backupHost. Cutting it therefore takes either blocking shareMount itself or blocking both printServer and backupHost. If shareMount is blocked, one remaining block cannot stop both vaultRead and dbReplica. If printServer and backupHost are blocked, nothing is left to stop dbReplica and codeRepo.\"}"
    }
   ],
